WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
<v Mike>The Last Ninja, battle your way to a showdown with the evil Shogun.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:30.160
<v Mike>And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.440
<v Hosts>I'm Mike.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.900
<v Hosts>I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.020
<v Mike>And today we are playing the definitive experience of what would happen if the last ninja showed

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.180
<v Mike>up in Central Park.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.800
<v Sean>You say, like, what would happen if the last ninja would show up in Central Park?

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.760
<v Sean>Like, as if the last ninja is somebody we should know already.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.180
<v Sean>Who was the last ninja?

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.420
<v Mike>No, the last ninja is, it's like something that will become known to us.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.400
<v Mike>We, there are, there are currently many ninjas.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.280
<v Mike>We don't know who's going to be the last.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:10.900
<v Sean>This is the last ninja who apparently is like a 40 year old kind of pudgy dude that just lives in New York City.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.620
<v Mike>Or, or got teleported there.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.500
<v Mike>Like, it's unclear how this game starts because it just throws you right into it.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.860
<v Mike>And you're like on this, you're on this box when, or like square when you start the game.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.760
<v Mike>And I thought that was like, oh, did he teleport here or something?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.760
<v Mike>Like, is that what, is that what's going on?

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.400
<v Mike>Is that why a ninja is in New York City of all places?

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.940
<v Sean>In broad daylight. Right.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:41.020
<v Mike>Is that why the UI has his face and a really crude drawing of the Statue of Liberty on it?

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.980
<v Mike>Like, is, is that what's going on here?

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.260
<v Mike>But, all right, I guess I'll find out what's going on.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.740
<v Mike>First off, hard to figure out what this game is without the manual.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.520
<v Mike>Like, you can't just, this is not one where you can just be like, oh, I'll load up the ROM and start playing it.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.580
<v Mike>It's like, you will not be able to start playing this game.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.760
<v Sean>So, I've.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.400
<v Mike>No, sure, you can.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.700
<v Mike>Yeah, it's not illegal.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:10.440
<v Mike>Like, like it is to be an, it is illegal to juggle milk bottles and throw them at ninjas in Central Park.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.020
<v Mike>That is a known illegal thing.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:26.400
<v Mike>Here, though, the problem is, is that if you do something like that, you might have an experience similar to mine where you leave that room and get to the next room and get into a fist fight with somebody who has unlimited HP.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.060
<v Mike>Like, you can't actually kill them.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.820
<v Mike>You can just only incapacitate them.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.500
<v Mike>But maybe that's because that's like the ninja code or something.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.180
<v Mike>And then there's this button on a wall.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.380
<v Mike>And, of course, you want to punch that button.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.520
<v Mike>Like, it's just, it's natural.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:49.400
<v Mike>So, I did the, I did the puzzle solving thing and I punched the button and it closed in and I could not for the life of me figure out what to do next.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:03:00.000
<v Mike>Because for some reason, my peanut sized brain couldn't think to go back to the other, only other room I'd ever been in in this game so far and be like, oh, I wonder if anything's different in there.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.240
<v Mike>I didn't do that.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:07.900
<v Mike>I never thought to do that for the 10 minutes that I was like then online and everything.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.600
<v Mike>And I was like, what is this game even?

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.500
<v Mike>I was reading the manual.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:20.220
<v Mike>And eventually I just watched a long play and said, oh, that room with the square that I thought was where you teleported from is actually outlined for a trap door.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.060
<v Sean>Yeah. And that's how you start the game.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.580
<v Sean>So, that's when you realized that you are playing basically a point and click adventure game with extra steps.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:39.380
<v Sean>And, again, like I think the craziest part about this game just is the whole scenario.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:46.800
<v Sean>Like you just are, you just are this ninja in modern day New York City.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.080
<v Sean>There are no other ninjas.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.520
<v Sean>There's no, there's no like league of ninjas.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.100
<v Sean>You're just the ninja.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.620
<v Joe>Well, you're the last one.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.180
<v Sean>Why would there be a league? Well, I mean, I guess you're right.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.960
<v Sean>You're right. That is in the title.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.980
<v Sean>But it's still like inexplicable that you are a ninja.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.560
<v Joe>Yeah, right, right.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:14.160
<v Sean>And it's all just these kind of like goofy situations, like puzzles that you have to solve.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:21.960
<v Sean>And, yeah, but it's more so because for a game that has so, like there is fighting.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.900
<v Sean>Like you do, like Mike was saying, you do incapacitate a guy.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.280
<v Sean>You can also just try and avoid them.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.440
<v Sean>So, there is some like press this button to attack.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.640
<v Sean>But they made two attack buttons.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.100
<v Sean>And then you, and this is why you can't really get too far in this game without looking at a manual.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:47.700
<v Sean>Is because you immediately have to start like pressing button combinations just to like get stuff out of your inventory.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.100
<v Sean>And it's just very strange.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:54.000
<v Joe>Yeah, I mean, I don't even think a manual is enough for me.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.440
<v Joe>I need a guide. Because I needed like this.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.200
<v Joe>It's just the point and click adventure-ness of it.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:05.220
<v Joe>And my brain cannot separate that from like all the shit I've got to do with this ninja at the time.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.820
<v Joe>So, like I'm not, I'm just focusing on like getting this ninja to like move where I wanted to move and to attack.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.840
<v Joe>So, then when I like get to the places, I'm like, I don't know.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:17.580
<v Joe>I wasn't paying attention to what's on the, you know, where the button is or whatever.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.580
<v Joe>So, I needed a guide to even get anywhere in this.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:28.040
<v Joe>But like, luckily, I will say that you mentioned that you could try to avoid people.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.820
<v Joe>You don't even have to try that hard.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.620
<v Joe>They don't really, you know, they don't really bother you if you don't bother them for the most part.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.320
<v Sean>I guess it depends on how lucky you get with like wherever they spawn or something.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.140
<v Sean>Because they will block you.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:48.920
<v Sean>And then you look like an idiot or at least I look like an idiot just jumping in place trying to get past these guys.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.840
<v Joe>Oh, yeah, yeah. You can get like cornered.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.280
<v Joe>Yeah. For sure. Yeah.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:59.460
<v Joe>So, but like if you just like don't engage with them from the very beginning, a lot of them are just like standing there.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.480
<v Joe>Some of them do come at you.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:12.900
<v Joe>But even when you are in a fight, what drove me crazy is like there's just nothing about these punches and kicks or anything about the way you're playing this game that makes you feel like a ninja.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.800
<v Joe>Like all the way back in like Kung Fu, you felt like cool when you were doing your kicks.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:23.340
<v Joe>Like this is just like it feels like I'm just standing there like, all right, like I got to position myself like right here so I can throw the punch right there.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.980
<v Joe>Okay. And now he's going to hit me a couple of times.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.160
<v Joe>Oh, I got to move over like one inch so I can kick.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.960
<v Joe>And like it's just like it feels like it doesn't feel good.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.420
<v Sean>It feels like I'm playing as myself.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.200
<v Sean>Like if I dressed up in a costume.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.880
<v Mike>And that's largely because of the isometric viewpoint, which we haven't brought up yet.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:43.500
<v Mike>But this game is another isometric game.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:53.160
<v Mike>And like that's what's making this so much weirder to navigate because I don't disagree with the point and click like analogy.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:07:07.060
<v Mike>But because this isn't a game where like you use a mouse and like pick up objects and have like clear commands because you're also like in a in an actual action game at the same time.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:18.720
<v Mike>Any kind of like combination of items or puzzle solving on top of being the character at the same time creates a very frustrating experience.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:27.580
<v Mike>Most of the times for actually solving the puzzles because like there's puzzles in games that are just basically like try to find the key so that you can open the door.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.360
<v Mike>And sometimes the key is just on the ground.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.080
<v Mike>Other times it's like a combination or something like this game has stuff like that.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:37.560
<v Mike>But then it also has like, OK, jump on this boat.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.380
<v Mike>Yeah, exactly. Don't even jump on this boat.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.360
<v Mike>How do you get the boat to move first?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:50.120
<v Mike>Well, you have to jump over this area of water that leads to another another screen.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.560
<v Mike>So you have to know that there's going to be water there in the first place.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:08:06.120
<v Mike>You have to jump from the other screen to then make a leap of faith to the next screen over so that you're in the jumping animations that you land in the little island and then take your stick, which you hopefully acquire because if you don't have the stick, you can't do this.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:16.200
<v Mike>And then nudge the boat and then the boat starts moving and then you go back to screens to where the boat is going to line up to line up your jump to land on the boat as it's sailing across.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.200
<v Mike>It's like, I mean, damn, pretty cool puzzle.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:23.000
<v Mike>Like it is involved, but like it's really hard to pull off.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:29.580
<v Sean>You will die trying to jump on the first boat many, many times before you get to that second.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.280
<v Mike>Like, why can't ninjas swim?

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.220
<v Sean>I mean, it's a well-known fact that.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.980
<v Sean>Yeah. Ninjas can't swim.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.660
<v Joe>Right. That's why there's only one left.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.560
<v Mike>Yeah, they all drowned.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.520
<v Sean>Since the floods.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:49.760
<v Mike>Yeah. Joe, you mentioned that you don't feel like a ninja in this game.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:50.600
<v Mike>And it is true.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:56.840
<v Mike>Like, I agree with Sean that, or maybe both of you said this, that like you can't avoid the enemies.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.480
<v Mike>You should avoid the enemies because they can't be knocked out.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:03.180
<v Mike>So you're going to keep going back to these screens anyway, and you do have a health bar and such.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.060
<v Mike>So you might as well avoid conflict when possible.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:13.940
<v Mike>So I guess in a way, the game is forcing you to be non-violent or maybe a little stealthy, but it should have went more in on the stealth.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.840
<v Mike>Wait, it should have went in on the stealth.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:23.640
<v Mike>You're a ninja. Like, what are you doing just walking around in broad daylight in Central Park and everybody's just like, yeah, this guy here again.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:33.500
<v Joe>Well, and, you know, I don't want to rule out the fact that, like, the gameplay being, like, you not feeling like a ninja might have been, like, tongue in cheek.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.480
<v Joe>You know, it might have been, like, yeah, you're the last ninja, and, like, look at this guy.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.120
<v Joe>He's an idiot. He's walking around in broad daylight.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.240
<v Sean>He looks like he's in, like, a Halloween costume.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.480
<v Joe>But, like, I don't think it's that crazy.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:49.980
<v Joe>I mean, the opening, like, intro screen made me think, oh, this is going to be a silly game, and it's, like, intended to be a comedy.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.260
<v Joe>Now, I didn't really get that while playing it, but, like, when I'm looking back right now at the game, I'm like, it really is.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:01.780
<v Joe>It's like the little, like, bamboo font and the music with, like, and the Fred and Wilma or whatever are the, like, high scores.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:11.980
<v Mike>Yeah, wait, wait, we got to talk about the high scores for a second because it is funny that it is Bert and Ernie as first and second place.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.660
<v Mike>Then Barney and Fred.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.540
<v Mike>So, we have Sesame Street and the Flintstones.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:25.800
<v Mike>Then it's Stan and Oliver, which is Stan Laurel and Oliver Hardy, two old-style comedians.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.800
<v Mike>Yes. And then it just turns into Hello Marco and Rex.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.860
<v Mike>Rex, like, well, who the hell are they?

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.420
<v Mike>Whoever Marco and Rex are just got immortalized next to some pretty important names.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.260
<v Sean>I'm trying to think it's their cats.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.220
<v Sean>Hello, our cats.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:49.000
<v Sean>Yeah. I think that there's definitely, that definitely leads me to believe that some of this is supposed to be funny.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:53.460
<v Sean>But a lot of this, like, I just, I can't see that they did this on purpose.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:11:01.260
<v Sean>Like, when you pick up an item, did anybody else just think he was just sort of, like, squatting on it and, like, picking it up with his butt?

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.320
<v Sean>Am I the only one that immediately jumped to this?

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.140
<v Sean>No, no, not at all.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.780
<v Sean>Okay. Just making sure.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.560
<v Mike>I think the game gets silly like that all the time, though.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:15.360
<v Mike>Like, there's that, there's a crocodile blocking the exit out of the sewers.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.820
<v Mike>And naturally, what would you do?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.720
<v Mike>You would set the crocodile on fire.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:26.180
<v Mike>Yes. You just throw a Molotov cocktail at it and the next thing you know, it's on fire and you're out of that room.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:35.720
<v Sean>Much like how ninjas can't swim, we do know that, like, the moral enemy of any crocodile is a Molotov cocktail.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.700
<v Mike>Right, or just fire in general.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:46.180
<v Mike>I've always said that, like, one of the scariest days of my life was when I was at Universal Theme Park and I was on the Jaws ride.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:52.540
<v Mike>And it was scary enough having, you know, a mechanical Jaws shark coming after you on the boat.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:12:00.140
<v Mike>But then at one point, the river that you're on, on the boat cruise, it lights on fire.

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.540
<v Mike>And I found out that you can have fire in water.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:06.240
<v Mike>And I was like, oh my God, like, we are so, like, this is possible?

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.900
<v Mike>Like, all of our worst fears are being realized if you could have fire on top of water.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:14.580
<v Sean>But that's when, that's only when the crocodiles harness that power.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.300
<v Sean>Like, usually they don't have that.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.400
<v Mike>Look it up, people.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:18.720
<v Mike>Fire on water.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:39.940
<v Mike>Scary stuff. All right, so the hook of this game, you know, whether it's the tone or the ridiculousness or being a ninja, the real game is about figuring out what object you need, where to use it, and how to position yourself so that the game understands that you're trying to use it.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.980
<v Mike>Because so much of this is, like, contextual.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:52.100
<v Mike>And I do think, like, if it was a, even followed more of the point and click commands and had, like, a, when you're near, let's say you're near a chest, right?

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.300
<v Mike>I don't even think there are chests in this game.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:13:01.120
<v Mike>But if there was, and you were able to then, like, navigate to a submenu for use and then key.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:08.920
<v Mike>Like, that would be better than having to cycle through this menu of just, your UI says you're using and you're holding.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:15.460
<v Mike>And using is, like, what you're using to attack and you're holding is the item that you're trying to use to solve the puzzle.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.040
<v Mike>It's just all a very, like, clunky experience.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:28.060
<v Sean>And when, and this is something I never truly understood, like, you always kind of default to using a ninja kicking.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.160
<v Sean>And there's always, like, a number next to that.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:34.560
<v Sean>What does that mean?

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.560
<v Joe>Do you know how many kicks you have left?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:44.620
<v Joe>Yeah, I thought that that was just, like, they ran out of real estate on this UI because of their giant ninja head in Statue of Liberty.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:50.960
<v Joe>So they just, like, had the using thing, but then, like, when you're done selecting it, it switches back to, like, oh, and this is how many lives you have.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.160
<v Sean>Okay. I thought it was lives.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.400
<v Sean>But I don't know. And, yeah, this is so strange.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:14:03.980
<v Sean>And then I started to think that, like, do you lose the item you were holding if you pick up another one?

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.520
<v Sean>Or is it just, like, you've got to start cycling through it again?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:11.980
<v Sean>Because I ended up, like, just dying so many times I could never really keep track of what my inventory ever was.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:18.880
<v Sean>But I remember, like, I picked up a key, and I needed to use that key to open up a gate.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:26.900
<v Sean>But then I tried as hard as I could to find that key, and I accidentally picked up, like, an egg muffin since.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.600
<v Sean>And I'm like, did I overwrite my key?

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:34.280
<v Mike>You're not thinking of the right button inputs, Sean.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.320
<v Mike>It's not simply enough to use select to cycle through them.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.600
<v Mike>You have to press select and the A button to cycle through what you're holding.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.940
<v Sean>It's so crazy.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.340
<v Mike>Because to cycle through what you're using, it's select and the B button.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:51.580
<v Mike>These are just normal things that everybody's come to understand in video games.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:56.860
<v Mike>We always cycle through our inventories with the select and B button and vice versa, with the A button.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.640
<v Sean>It's tough. It's very tough.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:05.620
<v Mike>I also don't like some of the, like, holding and then, like, just showing the picture of, like, the world's worst cheeseburger.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:07.160
<v Joe>What is that?

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:10.680
<v Mike>That actually looks like two pancakes with, like, some jam stuffed between them.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:11.680
